  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "@@map(\"users\") on a model and @map(\"created_at\") on a field are the same definition.config_mapping fact; the model-level one is told apart by definition.container naming the model, which is what prisma.model.table joins on, so @@map on a view or a composite type is still unstated -- their fields' names would have to be excluded the same way and the arrangement is rare",
      "the field names inside @relation(fields: [...], references: [...]) arrive as reference.field with definition.container naming the annotated field, and nothing separates the own-model foreign key column from the target-model referenced column, so no rule claims either; the model-level lists of @@id, @@unique and @@index are stated by prisma.model.constraint-column, but nothing in the fact says which of the three it was",
      "a setting whose value is an array, a number or a call -- previewFeatures = [\"views\"], url = env(...) -- is emitted by the second definition.config_setting template with no value field, so the setting is stated and its value is not; what env(...) holds is stated separately as an EnvVar",
      "computed Prisma Client/runtime query behavior, database introspection and generated client artifacts are runtime/external semantics"
